ata-e-type=\"section\" data-settings=\"{&quot;_ha_eqh_enable&quot;:false}\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-inner-column elementor-element elementor-element-3393911\" data-id=\"3393911\" data-element_type=\"column\" data-e-type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-1a84c9b elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"1a84c9b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p><strong>About the Cuilcagh Trek for World Suicide Prevention Day<\/strong><\/p><p>Since 2021 Aisling Centre has held an event to mark World Suicide Prevention Day on 10th of September. Members of the public, as well as volunteers and staff of Aisling Centre make the trek up Cuilcagh Mountain at the crack of Dawn.<\/p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">People choose to do the trek for many different and personal reasons. Some may come to remember a loved one, others as part of their own recovery, some may enjoy the challenge, while others will attend to show solidary and support for people who are struggling with their mental health. For everyone, it is an act of self-care, an opportunity to connect and ground themselves while enjoying the many benefits of being out in nature.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-50 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-97e0254\" data-id=\"97e0254\" data-element_type=\"column\" data-e-type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-a684d76 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\" data-id=\"a684d76\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"image.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"https:\/\/theaislingcentre.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/IMG_0066-1024x683.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-2122\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/theaislingcentre.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/IMG_0066-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/theaislingcentre.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/IMG_0066-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/theaislingcentre.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/IMG_0066-768x512.jpg 768w, https:\/\/theaislingcentre.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/IMG_0066-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/theaislingcentre.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/IMG_0066-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/theaislingcentre.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/IMG_0066-600x400.jpg 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-3cdb907 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"3cdb907\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-e-type=\"section\" data-settings=\"{&quot;_ha_eqh_enable&quot;:false}\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-50 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-acb056d\" data-id=\"acb056d\" data-element_type=\"column\" data-e-type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d071185 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\" data-id=\"d071185\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"image.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"https:\/\/theaislingcentre.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/IMG_0084crop-1024x683.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-2121\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/theaislingcentre.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/IMG_0084crop-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/theaislingcentre.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/IMG_0084crop-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/theaislingcentre.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/IMG_0084crop-768x512.jpg 768w, https:\/\/theaislingcentre.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/IMG_0084crop-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/theaislingcentre.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/IMG_0084crop-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/theaislingcentre.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/IMG_0084crop-600x400.jpg 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-50 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-f426964\" data-id=\"f426964\" data-element_type=\"column\" data-e-type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-565432a elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"565432a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>World Suicide Prevention Day, which first started in 2003, is observed across the world on 10th September annually. It aims to start a conversation about suicide and promote a worldwide message of Hope. Aisling Centre hope that organising this event will encourage people who may be considering ending their lives to talk to someone and to remind them that there is help available.<\/p><p>Locally along with Aisling Centre (028 66 325811) you can talk to your GP.\u00a0 The Samaritans (116 123) and Lifeline (0808 808 8000) helplines are available 24\/7.<\/p><p>\u00a0<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-2b681bb elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"2b681bb\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-e-type=\"section\" data-settings=\"{&quot;_ha_eqh_enable&quot;:false}\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-50 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-1fe4532\" data-id=\"1fe4532\" data-element_type=\"column\" data-e-type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6df02cf elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"6df02cf\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Cuilcagh Mountain stands 2,182ft (665 metres) above sea level.\u00a0 The Cuilcagh Boardwalk Trail showcases the scenic wilderness of the mountain and the breathtaking views of the surrounding lowlands. The Boardwalk Trail has made Cuilcagh Mountain so much more accessible however Iain Kennedy (Aisling Centre Fundraising Committee) advises that it remains a challenging trek and a reasonable level of fitness is needed. The distance of the mountain is approximately 8 miles (round trip). A person with a reasonable level of fitness should be able to complete the trek in approximately 3 hours. Alison Annan, Chairperson, Aisling Centre was delighted with the success of the event, \u201cIt is a really well supported event, and the weather has been kind to us\u201d. Feedback has been positive with Trekkers giving their vote of approval to the excellent organisation and care of the event with everything from the warm-up yoga to the breakfast at the end.<\/p><p>For any further information on this year&#8217;s event please contact Aisling Centre Tel: 028 66 325811 Email: info@theaislingcentre.com<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-50 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-4997ab5\" data-id=\"4997ab5\" data-element_type=\"column\" data-e-type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d144adc elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"d144adc\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p><em>\u201cThank you to all who were involved in organising this excellent event. I thoroughly enjoyed the morning\u201d<\/em><\/p><p><em>\u201cIt gave us both a sense of peace and calm in the midst of our grief.\u201d<\/em><\/p><p><em>\u201cVery inspiring seeing a lot of Aisling Centre team walk with us\u201d<\/em><\/p><p><em>\u201cWell done Shauna with the warm-up.\u201d<\/em><\/p><p><em>\u201cThe refreshments at the end were a particularly nice touch and totally unexpected\u201d<\/em><\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Cuilcagh Trek for World Suicide Prevention Day To book your place on our 2026 Cuilcagh Dawn Trek, please click the Check out but